//
// chunkRows > 0 caps each call and repeats until the backlog is drained, so a
// first pass over months of accumulated history is a series of bounded
// statements instead of one DELETE over the whole candidate set. Outside a
// transaction each chunk commits on its own, which is what keeps the lock hold
// and the WAL burst bounded; inside one (r.tx set) the chunks still bound each
// statement but commit together. chunkRows <= 0 prunes in a single call.
